WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.200
This session develops the advanced respiratory skills in the school reading table. The diagnostic lecture explained gases; now decide what the patient actually needs before the next laboratory result arrives.
本节展开学校阅读表中的高级呼吸技能。诊断课已解释血气，现在要判断下一化验出来前，患者真正需要什么。

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:27.072
Connect mechanism to a practical action: open and maintain the airway, improve effective airflow, support gas exchange and protect circulation. A better oxygen display is only one observation.
要把机制连到实际行动：开放并维持气道、改善有效气流、支持气体交换及保护循环。氧显示更好，只是一项观察。

00:00:27.072 --> 00:00:37.320
We will rehearse bronchodilator delivery, the full CPAP screen, PEEP during assisted ventilation and the decision to stop an ineffective or unsafe treatment.
我们会演练扩支气管给药、完整CPAP筛查、辅助通气时的PEEP，以及何时停止无效或不安全治疗。

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:49.368
Use the named local procedure and the actual equipment instructions together. The reading provides source detail; physical assembly and competence still require the school device and instructor.
应把点名当地规程与实际设备说明一起用。阅读提供来源细节，实体组装及能力仍需学校设备和教师确认。

00:00:49.368 --> 00:01:00.576
Assess patency and the ability to maintain and protect the airway. Speech, secretions, vomit and responsiveness can immediately change the support options.
应评气道通畅及维持保护能力。说话、分泌物、呕吐及反应，都能立即改变支持选择。

00:01:00.576 --> 00:01:12.264
Look at rate and depth together, listen for useful air entry and assess effort. A very rapid shallow pattern may move little effective air despite looking busy.
频率要与深度一起看，并听有效进气、评用力。极快浅呼吸虽然看起来忙，却可能几乎没有有效空气。

00:01:12.264 --> 00:01:22.224
Check circulation while respiratory care proceeds. Positive pressure, medication and the underlying illness may all affect pressure and perfusion.
呼吸照护同时检查循环。正压、药物及原病，都可能影响血压灌注。

00:01:22.224 --> 00:01:33.672
Treat immediate threats, request appropriate help and plan conveyance without making the distressed patient walk. Do not finish a long history before providing necessary support.
需处理即时威胁、请求适当支援并规划转运，不能让窘迫者走路，也不能先问完长病史才给必要支持。

00:01:33.672 --> 00:01:45.840
Respiratory distress describes increased work and difficulty. Respiratory failure means the required oxygenation or ventilation is not being maintained; the two can overlap.
呼吸窘迫描述功增加及困难。呼吸衰竭是所需氧合或通气无法维持，两者可以重叠。

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:56.712
A tiring patient may become less noisy and less active because effort is failing. Falling rate and a quieter chest are not automatically signs of recovery.
疲惫患者可因用力失败而变安静、活动减少。频率下降及胸部声音减弱，不自动表示恢复。

00:01:56.712 --> 00:02:09.456
Look for worsening responsiveness, shallow movement, poor air entry and deteriorating perfusion. These can demand assisted ventilation even if supplemental oxygen has improved saturation.
应找反应变差、运动浅、进气少及灌注恶化。即使补氧让饱和度好转，这些也可能要求辅助通气。

00:02:09.456 --> 00:02:19.992
Reassess after every meaningful change. A patient who initially qualified for CPAP can leave that branch when ventilation or airway protection deteriorates.
每次重要变化后都要复评。起初适合CPAP者，一旦通气或气道保护变差，就可能离开该分支。

00:02:19.992 --> 00:02:32.040
Obstructed airways increase resistance and make expiration difficult. Bronchospasm, edema, mucus and lost elastic support can contribute in different proportions.
阻塞气道增加阻力，让呼气困难。支气管痉挛、水肿、黏液及弹性支持丧失，可按不同比例参与。

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:43.728
Pulmonary edema adds fluid to the gas-exchange region and increases work. Positive pressure can help a selected patient, but the circulation still needs careful assessment.
肺水肿在交换区域增加液体并增加功。正压可帮助选定患者，但循环仍需仔细评估。

00:02:43.728 --> 00:02:56.904
Embolism, pneumonia, pneumothorax, anemia and metabolic acidosis can also present with breathlessness. Neither wheeze nor crackles identifies one disease by itself.
栓塞、肺炎、气胸、贫血及代谢性酸中毒，也可表现气促。喘鸣或湿啰音，单独都不能确定一种病。

00:02:56.904 --> 00:03:06.528
State the leading mechanism and a dangerous alternative. This keeps treatment patient-specific when cardiac and respiratory disease coexist.
应说出首要机制及一个危险鉴别。这样心肺疾病并存时，治疗仍能针对患者。

00:03:06.528 --> 00:03:18.288
Asthma combines variable bronchoconstriction with inflammation and mucus. A bronchodilator may quickly address one component without instantly clearing all obstruction.
哮喘结合可变支气管收缩、炎症及黏液。扩支气管药可能较快处理其中一项，却不能立刻清除全部阻塞。

00:03:18.288 --> 00:03:29.832
Expiration becomes prolonged and the next inspiration can begin before emptying is complete. Explain this mechanism instead of merely memorizing an increased-work label.
呼气延长，下次吸气可在排空前就开始。应解释这个机制，而不只背呼吸功增加。

00:03:29.832 --> 00:03:39.648
Wheeze requires moving air. A severe presentation with a silent chest or barely audible air entry can be more dangerous than a loud wheeze.
喘鸣需要流动空气。严重表现伴静默胸或几乎听不到进气，可能比响亮喘鸣更危险。

00:03:39.648 --> 00:03:51.912
Use brief assessment, prompt appropriate treatment and repeated functional reassessment. Do not assume every ambulance asthma call has the same severity or a proven status diagnosis.
应简短评估、及时适当治疗并反复评功能。不能假定每个哮喘呼叫严重度相同，或已证实持续状态。

00:03:51.912 --> 00:04:05.184
Prior intensive care, intubation or repeated severe exacerbations raise concern. Ask these questions early without requiring a breathless patient to recite a complete medical biography.
既往ICU、插管或反复严重加重，会增加担忧。应尽早问，但不要求气促者背完整病史。

00:04:05.184 --> 00:04:15.216
Find out how much rescue medicine was used and whether it helped. Increasing use with shrinking benefit is more useful than the name of an inhaler alone.
要查用了多少急救药、是否有效。用量增加而收益缩小，比只知道吸入器名称更有用。

00:04:15.216 --> 00:04:26.520
Ask about fever, exposures, empty devices and barriers to treatment. Use neutral language rather than assuming missed treatment reflects rebellion or indifference.
应问发热、暴露、设备空及治疗障碍。用中性语言，不假定漏治疗就是反抗或不在乎。

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:36.312
Obtain relevant action-plan and treatment-limit information when available. These inform the pathway but do not replace assessment of the current threat.
有资料时取得相关行动计划及治疗限制。这些会影响路径，但不能替代评当前威胁。

00:04:36.312 --> 00:04:48.720
Emphysematous destruction reduces elastic recoil and gas-exchange surface. Chronic bronchitic disease adds inflammation and mucus; many patients have overlapping features.
肺气肿性破坏减少弹性回缩及交换面积。慢性支气管炎增加炎症黏液，许多患者特征重叠。

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:58.608
A new stressor acts on limited reserve. Infection is common, but a cardiac event, pneumothorax or equipment problem may be contributing.
新压力作用于有限储备。感染常见，但心脏事件、气胸或设备问题也可能参与。

00:04:58.608 --> 00:05:10.200
Rapid breathing does not exclude dangerous hypercapnia. Small ineffective breaths, dead space, obstruction and fatigue can reduce useful alveolar ventilation.
呼吸快不能排除危险高碳酸。浅小无效呼吸、死腔、阻塞及疲劳，都可减少有效肺泡通气。

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:22.584
Ask about usual exercise tolerance, saturation, oxygen and support. The important story is how the current function differs, not whether the patient matches a body-shape stereotype.
应问平时活动耐受、饱和度、给氧及支持。重要的是现在功能与平常有何不同，而非是否符合某种体型刻板印象。

00:05:22.584 --> 00:05:34.560
Known COPD does not exclude acute coronary disease or pulmonary edema. Chest discomfort may be absent, and breathlessness may be the dominant cardiac symptom.
已有COPD也不能排除急性冠脉或肺水肿。胸部不适可能缺如，气促可以是主要心脏症状。

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:48.000
Sudden deterioration, unequal air entry, trauma or new pressure changes should reopen the differential. Do not keep increasing positive pressure without considering pneumothorax and perfusion.
突然恶化、进气不对称、创伤或新血压变化，应重开鉴别。不能不想气胸及灌注，就持续加正压。

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:58.368
Deep rapid breathing can be compensation for metabolic acidosis. Suppressing it or assuming anxiety because the rate is high can worsen the underlying problem.
深快呼吸可代偿代谢性酸中毒。仅因频率快就抑制它或假定焦虑，会加重原问题。

00:05:58.368 --> 00:06:08.976
Check the equipment path as well as disease. A disconnected tube and a severe illness can coexist; repairing one does not prove the other has resolved.
除了病，也要检查设备路径。管脱开可与严重疾病并存，修好一项不证明另一项已解决。

00:06:08.976 --> 00:06:19.176
The checked COPD guidance generally targets eighty-eight to ninety-two percent. Patient baseline and the actual clinical state provide additional context.
核对的COPD指导一般目标88%至92%，患者基线及真实临床状态还提供额外背景。

00:06:19.176 --> 00:06:29.184
This is different from the school post-ROSC target of ninety-four to ninety-eight. Targets are not interchangeable simply because both involve breathlessness.
它不同于学校ROSC后94%至98%的目标。不能因都涉及呼吸问题，就互换目标。

00:06:29.184 --> 00:06:41.880
Never deny needed oxygen or assisted ventilation because of a simplistic hypoxic-drive explanation. Treat immediate hypoxemia while monitoring the whole patient and titrating appropriately.
绝不能因简单低氧驱动解释而拒给必要氧或辅助通气。应纠正即时低氧，监测整位患者并适当滴定。

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:52.920
Saturation does not measure carbon-dioxide clearance. A rising oxygen number with worsening fatigue needs a new ventilation decision, not congratulations.
饱和度不测CO2清除。氧数字上升却越来越疲惫，需重新决定通气，而非当作成功。

00:06:52.920 --> 00:07:03.984
Poor perfusion, movement, a poor probe fit or cold extremities can compromise oximetry. Check signal quality and whether the displayed pulse plausibly matches the patient.
灌注差、运动、探头不合或末梢冷，可妨碍脉氧。应核信号质量，并看显示脉率是否与患者相符。

00:07:03.984 --> 00:07:16.056
A reliable saturation still does not describe hemoglobin amount or effective blood flow. An anemic or shocked patient can have inadequate delivery despite an acceptable percentage.
即使饱和度可靠，也不描述血红蛋白数量或有效血流。贫血或休克者，百分比尚可仍可能输氧不足。

00:07:16.056 --> 00:07:28.896
Capnography adds information about ventilation, perfusion and the sampling path. A sudden change must be linked to the patient and circuit rather than read as a stand-alone diagnosis.
二氧化碳波形增加通气、灌注及取样路径信息。突然变化应联系患者和回路，不能当独立诊断。

00:07:28.896 --> 00:07:37.944
Do not postpone necessary support while trying to perfect an instrument reading. Treat the credible clinical threat while troubleshooting safely.
不能为追求完美仪器读数而推迟必要支持。应在安全排错同时处理可信的临床威胁。

00:07:37.944 --> 00:07:49.104
With obstruction, exhalation may remain incomplete when the next breath begins. Repeated excessive breaths can progressively increase trapped volume and pressure.
阻塞时，下一呼吸开始，前次呼气可能仍未完成。反复过量通气可逐渐增加潴留容积及压力。

00:07:49.104 --> 00:07:58.632
Raised intrathoracic pressure can impair venous return, lower pressure and make further ventilation difficult. Barotrauma is another concern.
胸内压升高可妨碍回心血、降低血压并使后续通气更难，也需担忧压力伤。

00:07:58.632 --> 00:08:12.336
Use effective airway positioning, seal and appropriate assistance, allowing exhalation and reassessing response. More force and a faster rate are not automatic answers to every poor oxygen number.
应有效摆气道、密封并适当辅助，留呼气时间且复评反应。不是氧数字差，就自动更用力更快吹。

00:08:12.336 --> 00:08:24.480
The rate depends on age, spontaneous effort, arrest state and the authorized pathway. Do not copy an isolated old textbook rate as a universal rule for severe COPD.
频率依年龄、自主用力、是否骤停及获授权路径决定。不能照抄旧教材孤立频率，作为严重COPD通用规则。

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:35.256
When breathing is inadequate, support ventilation promptly through the appropriate airway pathway. Do not wait for a steroid, a gas result or a better CPAP fit.
呼吸不足时，需及时依适当气道路径支持通气。不能等激素、血气或更好的CPAP适配。

00:08:35.256 --> 00:08:45.720
Position the airway, clear obstruction and use indicated adjuncts. A second trained provider can help maintain the seal and airway while the other manages the bag.
应摆好气道、清阻塞并用有指征辅助物。第二名受训者可维持密封气道，另一人管囊。

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:57.072
Deliver effective breaths with visible chest movement, without excessive volume or rate. Check that the chest can fall and air can leave, particularly in obstruction.
给有效呼吸，让胸部可见运动，但不过量过快。尤其阻塞时，应看胸能下降、空气能排出。

00:08:57.072 --> 00:09:09.048
Reassess oxygen supply, connections, air entry and circulation. An added valve cannot repair an obstructed airway, empty cylinder or poor basic ventilation.
需复评氧源、连接、进气及循环。加阀不能修气道阻塞、空氧瓶或差基础通气。

00:09:09.048 --> 00:09:20.328
Salbutamol relaxes bronchial smooth muscle through beta-two stimulation. Its effect is relevant when bronchospasm contributes, not every cause of breathlessness.
沙丁胺醇通过β2刺激松弛支气管平滑肌。支气管痉挛参与时相关，但不能处理所有气促病因。

00:09:20.328 --> 00:09:32.400
Ipratropium reduces muscarinic bronchoconstrictor activity and complements salbutamol. The local acute regimen uses one dose rather than an automatic dose with every repeat.
异丙托溴铵减少毒蕈碱性缩支气管活动，与沙丁胺醇互补。当地急性方案只单次，不是每轮重复都自动加。

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:44.304
Dexamethasone addresses inflammation over hours. A patient in immediate ventilatory failure needs support now, not observation until the anti-inflammatory effect peaks.
地塞米松在数小时内处理炎症。即时通气衰竭患者现在就需支持，不能观察到抗炎峰值。

00:09:44.304 --> 00:09:56.256
Mechanism guides the reassessment: ask whether air movement, effort, symptoms and perfusion improved, and whether an adverse effect or alternative diagnosis is emerging.
机制指导复评：应问气流、用力、症状灌注是否改善，有无出现不良作用或其他诊断。

00:09:56.256 --> 00:10:06.960
Confirm the medicine and strength, expiry and remaining doses. Propellant or a shaking sound alone does not prove useful medicine remains.
需确认药名浓度、有效期及剩余剂量。仅有推进剂或摇动声，不证明仍有有效药。

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:17.544
Prepare the actual inhaler and spacer as instructed. Check the mouthpiece and connection, and explain the inhalation technique before dispensing the dose.
应依说明准备真实吸入器及储雾罐，核口器和连接，并在释药前解释吸入方法。

00:10:17.544 --> 00:10:27.744
Use one actuation at a time with the device-specific inhalation method. Do not discharge several puffs together or leave a prepared cloud waiting for minutes.
应依装置吸入法逐喷给药，不能几喷一起打，或把准备的雾云放几分钟等着。

00:10:27.744 --> 00:10:39.720
Observe whether the patient can actually inhale the dose and reassess response. If effort or consciousness fails, change the support plan rather than repeating an ineffective ritual.
要观察患者是否真能吸入并复评反应。若用力或意识失败，应改支持计划，而非重复无效仪式。

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:51.960
Check the product, dose and units before adding medication. Micrograms and milligrams are not interchangeable, and premixed products must be identified rather than guessed.
加药前应核产品、剂量及单位。微克与毫克不能互换，预混产品也必须认清，不能猜。

00:10:51.960 --> 00:11:03.288
Use the actual nebulizer operating flow and a suitable patient interface. Mist escaping while the patient turns away does not establish the intended lung dose.
应使用真实雾化器工作流量及合适患者接口。患者转头、雾跑出去，不证明预期剂量已进肺。

00:11:03.288 --> 00:11:15.720
Apply indicated infection-control precautions. An MDI with spacer is preferred in some infectious circumstances, but the choice still depends on appropriate delivery and the actual pathway.
需落实有指征感染防护。有些感染情境更倾向MDI加储雾罐，但仍需考虑适当给药及真实路径。

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:26.424
Monitor oxygenation and ventilation throughout treatment. The nebulizer label does not guarantee a universal inspired oxygen percentage or adequate breathing.
治疗全程需监测氧合通气。雾化器名称不保证通用吸入氧百分比或足够呼吸。

00:11:26.424 --> 00:11:37.752
The current adult monograph lists five milligrams nebulized, repeated back-to-back as needed, or four one-hundred-microgram actuations with spacer, repeated as needed.
现行成人专论列雾化5 mg，按需接续重复；或加储雾罐，每喷100微克共四喷，按需重复。

00:11:37.752 --> 00:11:48.960
The route-specific dose must match the actual product and authorized indication. Do not substitute the chronic home frequency or an adult dose for a pediatric calculation.
途径特定剂量必须对应真实产品及获授权指征。不能换成慢性居家频率，或给儿科套成人量。

00:11:48.960 --> 00:12:01.776
Look for improved air movement and reduced effort, but also tremor, tachycardia, dysrhythmia or paradoxical worsening. Beta-two selectivity does not mean zero systemic effect.
应看气流改善及功减少，也要找震颤、心动过速、心律失常或反常恶化。β2选择性不是完全无全身作用。

00:12:01.776 --> 00:12:13.776
High-dose nebulized treatment for hyperkalemia is separately listed at ACP level. It is not a second PCP bronchospasm dose available just because the medication is familiar.
高剂量雾化治高钾，另列ACP层级。不能因药熟悉，就当成另一可选PCP支气管痉挛剂量。

00:12:13.776 --> 00:12:24.600
The checked adult local dose is five hundred micrograms nebulized, or eight twenty-microgram actuations by MDI, totaling one hundred sixty micrograms.
核对的当地成人量为雾化500微克，或MDI每喷20微克共八喷，总160微克。

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:34.584
It is an adjunct single dose. Salbutamol may be repeated as indicated, but this does not authorize repeated ipratropium with each cycle.
这是辅助单次剂量。沙丁胺醇可按指征重复，但不授权每轮都重复异丙托溴铵。

00:12:34.584 --> 00:12:44.808
Pediatric dose and consultation requirements are different, and the source excludes neonates under thirty days. Do not let the adult card erase those gates.
儿科剂量及咨询要求不同，来源排除不足30日新生儿。成人卡不能抹去这些关卡。

00:12:44.808 --> 00:12:57.000
Protect the eyes and consider relevant glaucoma and urinary-retention cautions. Report actual response or paradoxical worsening rather than assuming more medicine is always needed.
应保护眼并注意相关青光眼和尿潴留慎用。要报告真实反应或反常恶化，不能总假定需要更多药。

00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:10.224
The checked monograph considers dexamethasone for known asthma or COPD with inadequate improvement after salbutamol and ipratropium. Confirm the actual indication, not wheeze alone.
核对专论对已知哮喘或COPD，在沙丁胺醇及异丙托溴铵后改善不足时考虑地塞米松。应核真实指征，不能只凭喘鸣。

00:13:10.224 --> 00:13:24.168
Adult PCP dosing is eight milligrams intravenously or orally, with oral preferred and prior CliniCall required. Verify the vial concentration rather than assuming all stock has one strength.
成人PCP量为静脉或口服8 mg，优先口服，给前必须CliniCall。应核瓶浓度，不能假定库存都一种规格。

00:13:24.168 --> 00:13:36.648
Clinical effect is delayed: up to two hours intravenously and two to six hours orally in the monograph. Continue necessary respiratory support while the drug has not yet acted.
专论列临床作用延迟，静脉可达两小时，口服二至六小时。药尚未起效时，仍需持续必要呼吸支持。

00:13:36.648 --> 00:13:50.592
Check contraindications, cautions and the patient context. A steroid does not make CPAP safe for a failing airway, and a suspected infection is not a blanket ban on every COPD steroid plan.
要核禁忌、慎用及患者背景。激素不能使气道失败者适合CPAP，疑感染也不是所有COPD激素计划的笼统禁止。

00:13:50.592 --> 00:14:03.792
Severe obstruction with exhaustion, deteriorating consciousness or very poor air entry requires urgent escalation. Do not wait for saturation to become extreme before recognizing failing function.
严重阻塞伴疲竭、意识恶化或进气极差，需紧急升级。不能等饱和度极端，才承认功能失败。

00:14:03.792 --> 00:14:13.944
Continue effective airway and ventilation support while arranging appropriate help and conveyance. Avoid unnecessary exertion or lengthy testing.
安排适当支援及转运时，持续有效气道通气支持，避免不必要活动或冗长检测。

00:14:13.944 --> 00:14:46.584
For selected severe asthma or impending respiratory arrest, the checked adult PCP epinephrine entry is zero point five milligrams intramuscularly every five to twenty minutes, with prior CliniCall recommended. Verify the actual indication and product concentration. This is not the anaphylaxis repeat schedule or an intravenous arrest dose. Pediatric weight-based dosing is separately stated in the bilingual reading; the adult repeat interval is not automatically imported.
对选定严重哮喘或濒临呼吸骤停，核对的成人PCP肾上腺素条目为肌注0.5 mg，每5至20分钟，给前建议CliniCall。须核真实指征及产品浓度；这不是过敏反应重复安排或静脉骤停剂量。儿科按体重用法另在双语阅读中说明，不能自动套成人重复间隔。

00:14:46.584 --> 00:14:59.208
IV epinephrine, magnesium and intubation are different advanced actions. Understanding why they may be used does not grant a PCP a new medication or airway permission.
静脉肾上腺素、镁及插管，是不同高级行动。懂其可能用途，不会给PCP新的药物或气道权限。

00:14:59.208 --> 00:15:11.568
Pulmonary edema impairs gas exchange and increases respiratory work. Ask whether a failing pump or another process explains the presentation, and check pressure and perfusion.
肺水肿妨碍交换并增加呼吸功。应问是否泵衰或其他过程解释表现，并核血压灌注。

00:15:11.568 --> 00:15:21.816
A tolerated upright position can help an appropriate patient, but do not impose it on an unconscious or shocked person regardless of airway and circulation needs.
适合患者可从耐受坐位获益，但不能不管气道循环需要，强加给无意识或休克者。

00:15:21.816 --> 00:15:48.360
Selected CPAP can recruit lung and reduce work. C06 places pulmonary-edema nitroglycerin under advanced care paramedic interventions. A PCP must not create a new pulmonary-edema nitrate order merely by passing the separate acute-coronary-syndrome pressure screen. Indication, role, exclusions and consultation all matter; crackles alone are not enough.
选定CPAP可募集肺并减轻功。C06把肺水肿硝酸甘油列在ACP干预下，PCP不能仅通过另一个急性冠脉综合征血压筛查，就创造肺水肿硝酸酯指令。指征、角色、排除和咨询都重要，湿啰音单独不够。

00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:58.896
Do not copy an older automatic fluid, furosemide or morphine list. Mechanism, current physiology, role and response determine the safe pathway.
不能照搬旧的自动补液、呋塞米或吗啡清单。机制、当前生理、角色及反应，共同决定安全路径。

00:15:58.896 --> 00:16:08.544
First ask whether spontaneous breathing is adequate enough for a noninvasive CPAP strategy. An oxygen deficit alone does not answer that question.
先问自主呼吸是否足够，能否采用无创CPAP策略。仅有氧不足，不能回答这个问题。

00:16:08.544 --> 00:16:18.384
When breathing is inadequate, use effective assisted ventilation through the appropriate airway pathway. CPAP does not provide missing rescue breaths.
呼吸不足时，应依适当气道路径有效辅助通气。CPAP不能补上缺失的救援呼吸。

00:16:18.384 --> 00:16:28.512
If hypoxemia persists despite good bag-mask technique and an appropriate airway, consider the separate PEEP procedure only after its own exclusions are checked.
良好BVM及适当气道后仍低氧，只有核完PEEP本身排除条件，才考虑这一独立规程。

00:16:28.512 --> 00:16:38.856
Every branch includes repeated assessment and a stop plan. A device selected ten minutes ago is not guaranteed to be correct after the patient changes.
每个分支都包括反复评估及停止计划。十分钟前选对的装置，患者变化后不保证仍对。

00:16:38.856 --> 00:16:49.032
CPAP maintains positive airway pressure while the patient breathes spontaneously. It can keep more alveoli available and reduce the work of a selected patient.
CPAP在患者自主呼吸时维持正压，可让更多肺泡可用，并减少选定患者的功。

00:16:49.032 --> 00:17:00.720
It is not the same as bilevel pressure support, and it does not deliver mandatory breaths to an apneic person. Names containing positive pressure are not interchangeable modes.
它不等于双水平压力支持，也不给无呼吸者强制呼吸。名称带正压，不表示模式可互换。

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:10.968
Positive pressure can reduce venous return and blood pressure. A treatment that helps oxygenation may become unsafe if circulation deteriorates.
正压可减少回心血及血压。即使帮助氧合，循环恶化后也可能不安全。

00:17:10.968 --> 00:17:21.864
Explain the intended benefit and the risk before fitting the mask. A successful procedure includes physiological benefit and tolerability, not merely a tight seal.
戴面罩前应解释预期收益及风险。成功规程包括生理获益和耐受，不能只有密封很紧。

00:17:21.864 --> 00:17:30.432
The checked entry screen requires a patient at least thirteen years old who is awake, follows commands and can maintain an open airway.
核对的进入筛查要求至少13岁、清醒、能遵指令并维持开放气道。

00:17:30.432 --> 00:17:43.752
It also lists all three respiratory findings: rate above twenty-four, saturation below ninety-four percent on oxygen and accessory-muscle use. Any one finding alone is not the full screen.
还列三项全部呼吸表现：频率大于24、补氧后饱和度低于94%，及辅助肌使用。任一项单独不算完整筛查。

00:17:43.752 --> 00:17:56.904
Check the actual indication and operator training requirement. Prior CliniCall is recommended in PR09; that recommendation is distinct from a mandatory medication consultation gate.
应核真实指征及操作者培训要求。PR09建议给前CliniCall，这个建议不同于药物的强制咨询关卡。

00:17:56.904 --> 00:18:07.656
Eligibility is only the beginning. The contraindication screen, patient consent, equipment and reassessment plan must also be satisfactory before starting.
符合资格只是开始。启动前还必须通过禁忌筛查，并有患者同意、设备及复评计划。

00:18:07.656 --> 00:18:19.584
Exclude apnea, hypoventilation and impending failure with slowing shallow effort or falling consciousness. CPAP is not a substitute for effective assisted ventilation.
应排除无呼吸、低通气，以及用力变慢变浅或意识下降的濒临失败。CPAP不能替代有效辅助通气。

00:18:19.584 --> 00:18:31.584
Vomiting or aspiration risk and inability to protect the airway can make a strapped mask unsafe. Prepare the alternative rather than hoping a better oxygen reading will cancel the risk.
呕吐、误吸风险及不能保护气道，会让束带面罩不安全。应备替代方案，不能希望更好的氧值抵消风险。

00:18:31.584 --> 00:18:42.792
The listed exclusions include systolic pressure below ninety, suspected pneumothorax, traumatic respiratory distress, tracheostomy and inability to obtain a proper fit.
所列排除包括收缩压低于90、疑气胸、创伤呼吸窘迫、气切及无法适配。

00:18:42.792 --> 00:18:54.360
Age and ability to follow commands remain relevant. Repeat the screen as the patient changes; absence of a contraindication at the start does not guarantee continued safety.
年龄及遵指令能力仍重要。患者变化后应重筛，开始无禁忌不保证之后一直安全。

00:18:54.360 --> 00:19:05.256
Explain what the mask will feel like, obtain appropriate consent and choose a tolerated position. Record baseline respiratory function, pressure and perfusion.
应解释面罩感觉、取得适当同意并选耐受体位，记录基线呼吸功能、血压及灌注。

00:19:05.256 --> 00:19:17.328
Identify the actual kit and check its assembly instructions, connections, valve, mask and pressure-flow chart. Do not transfer a remembered flow setting from another device.
要认清真实套件，核组装说明、连接、阀、面罩及压力流量图。不能从另一设备照搬记忆流量。

00:19:17.328 --> 00:19:27.912
Estimate oxygen availability for treatment and transport, including anticipated flow changes. A plan that exhausts the cylinder before arrival is incomplete.
应估计治疗和转运所需氧，包含可能调流。到院前耗空氧瓶的计划是不完整的。

00:19:27.912 --> 00:19:38.784
Have suction, effective bag-mask support, monitoring and a clear escalation plan ready. Assign who will manage the airway if CPAP must be removed immediately.
应备好吸引、有效BVM支持、监测及明确升级计划，并分配紧急移除CPAP时谁管气道。

00:19:38.784 --> 00:19:51.288
Start with the procedure-specified low setup for the actual device. PR09 describes five liters per minute if possible, otherwise six; the generated pressure depends on the equipment.
应依真实设备规程指定低起始设定。PR09描述可行时每分钟5升，否则6；产生压力依设备决定。

00:19:51.288 --> 00:20:03.984
Let the awake patient hold the mask initially when feasible, then progress to the indicated securing method. Coaching and consent can improve tolerance more safely than immediate force.
可行时先让清醒患者自己持面罩，再逐渐固定。指导及同意，比一开始强压更能安全改善耐受。

00:20:03.984 --> 00:20:14.928
Check fit and leaks without over-tightening. Follow the actual bonnet or strap design rather than improvising a way that creates pressure injury or blocks access.
要核适配漏气但不过紧，依真实帽或带设计，不能自创造成压伤或妨碍接近患者的固定法。

00:20:14.928 --> 00:20:26.400
Immediately reassess breathing, responsiveness, saturation, pressure and perfusion. If the patient cannot tolerate or safely use the interface, change the plan.
应立即重评呼吸、反应、饱和度、血压及灌注。患者不能耐受或安全使用接口时，应改计划。

00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:38.712
The saved examination sequence begins at five centimeters of water pressure. Use the actual manufacturer relationship between flow and pressure rather than equating liters with centimeters.
保存考试顺序从5厘米水柱开始。应依实际厂商流量压力关系，不能把升等同厘米。

00:20:38.712 --> 00:20:51.720
The current PR09 escalation wording uses saturation remaining below ninety-two percent. That differs from the entry criterion below ninety-four on oxygen; keep the two decisions distinct.
现行PR09升级措辞使用饱和度持续低于92%。这不同于补氧后低于94%的进入条件，两种决定应分开。

00:20:51.720 --> 00:21:03.432
When indicated, titrate through the device chart in the stated pressure steps, reassessing after changes. Flow adjustments may change both pressure and delivered oxygen.
有指征时，依设备图按规定压力步长滴定，并在改变后复评。调流可能同时改变压力及给氧。

00:21:03.432 --> 00:21:12.600
The treatment maximum is ten centimeters of water. Higher settings printed on an equipment table do not authorize exceeding the clinical ceiling.
治疗最高为10厘米水柱。设备表印了更高设定，不授权超过临床上限。

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:23.256
Assess air movement and work, not just saturation. The intended outcome is improved effective function without new fatigue or loss of airway protection.
要评气流及功，而不只饱和度。目标是有效功能改善，且不出现新疲劳或气道保护丧失。

00:21:23.256 --> 00:21:33.912
Continue to check responsiveness and ability to follow commands. New drowsiness can move the patient out of the CPAP branch even if the mask remains well sealed.
需持续核反应及遵指令能力。即使面罩密封仍好，新嗜睡也可让患者离开CPAP分支。

00:21:33.912 --> 00:21:45.048
Repeat pressure and perfusion assessment because positive pressure can reduce preload. Do not accept a rising oxygen number as permission to ignore falling circulation.
应重复评血压灌注，因为正压可降低前负荷。不能因氧数字上升，就忽视循环下降。

00:21:45.048 --> 00:21:56.328
Trace the device and oxygen path, preserving access to the patient. Document actual observations and settings so the next team can understand both benefit and risk.
需追查设备及氧路径，保留接近患者的空间。要记录真实观察和设定，让下一团队理解收益及风险。

00:21:56.328 --> 00:22:06.960
Deteriorating breathing, consciousness, pressure or airway protection requires immediate reassessment. Do not tighten the mask and wait for the number to recover.
呼吸、意识、血压或气道保护恶化，需立即复评。不能把面罩拉紧，然后等数字恢复。

00:22:06.960 --> 00:22:17.688
Remove an unsafe CPAP interface and provide appropriate airway and assisted-ventilation support. Keep suction and a trained second provider available where possible.
应移除不安全CPAP接口，并给适当气道及辅助通气支持，可行时备吸引及第二名受训者。

00:22:17.688 --> 00:22:27.480
PEEP is a separate choice with separate exclusions. A patient failing CPAP does not automatically qualify for every form of additional positive pressure.
PEEP是独立选择，有独立排除。CPAP失败者，不会自动适合所有额外正压。

00:22:27.480 --> 00:22:39.576
Escalate and communicate the actual change, previous settings, stop time and current support. Preserve the sequence so a harmful treatment is not inadvertently restarted.
应升级并沟通真实变化、先前设定、停止时间及当前支持。要保留顺序，避免无意重启有害治疗。

00:22:39.576 --> 00:22:52.008
PR10 considers PEEP when saturation remains below ninety despite good bag-mask technique and an appropriate airway. Fix basic ventilation problems before assuming more pressure is needed.
PR10在良好BVM及适当气道后饱和度仍低于90时考虑PEEP。应先修基础通气问题，不能假定需要更大压力。

00:22:52.008 --> 00:23:07.992
Screen the full exclusions, including cardiac arrest, suspected pneumothorax, traumatic respiratory arrest and the specified pressure limits. The exact-age-twelve wording gap requires clarification, not an invented pediatric rule.
应筛全部排除，包括心脏骤停、疑气胸、创伤呼吸骤停及所列血压限制。恰好12岁的措辞空隙应澄清，不能自创儿科规则。

00:23:07.992 --> 00:23:20.616
Use the proper exhaust valve, start at five and increase by two point five if indicated, to no more than ten. Maintain effective seal, appropriate ventilation and time for exhalation.
应使用适当排气阀，从5开始，有指征每次加2.5，不超过10，并维持有效密封、适当通气及呼气时间。

00:23:20.616 --> 00:23:34.344
Monitor pressure and oxygenation; remove for the specified hypotension, a new contraindication or equipment issue. CliniCall is required when hypoxemia persists despite maximal oxygen.
需监测血压氧合，按规定在低血压、新禁忌或设备问题时移除。最大给氧后仍低氧，要求CliniCall。

00:23:34.344 --> 00:23:44.304
The entry and escalation thresholds serve different questions. Do not replace both with a new halfway number or select whichever permits the intervention you want.
进入及升级阈值回答不同问题。不能取中间值替代，也不能挑一条允许自己想做的干预。

00:23:44.304 --> 00:23:57.744
PR10 excludes older-than-twelve patients at systolic pressure at or below ninety, while its removal sentence says below ninety. Record the wording difference and do not invent a permissive loophole.
PR10对大于12岁者，进入排除用收缩压小于等于90，移除句则用低于90。要记录措辞差异，不能自创允许治疗的漏洞。

00:23:57.744 --> 00:24:07.608
The school oxygen target, COPD target and resuscitation targets also have different contexts. State the named pathway whenever using a number.
学校给氧、COPD及复苏目标也有不同背景。每次用数字，都应说清点名路径。

00:24:07.608 --> 00:24:20.664
If school device instructions or an assessed rubric are missing, preserve that gap. A precise theory rehearsal is useful, but it is not evidence that an unseen assembly step was taught correctly.
若缺学校设备说明或考核表，应保留缺口。准确理论演练有用，但不能证明未见组装步骤已正确教授。

00:24:20.664 --> 00:25:04.536
Use WHIPS to focus the severe-bronchospasm history: worst episode, hospital visits, ICU stays, puffer requirements and steroid requirements. Ask questions answerable with a word or head movement while support continues. That history helps anticipate deterioration rather than merely assigning a severity label. Salbutamol may briefly provoke cough or louder sounds; distinguish this from falling air entry, exhaustion or reduced awareness. A rapidly worsening patient needs immediate reassessment and support, not a rule to wait until every nebulizer finishes. Follow the indicated refusal process if conveyance is declined.
用WHIPS聚焦严重支气管痉挛病史：是否最严重一次、医院就诊、ICU经历、急救吸入药需求及激素需求。支持持续进行时，问题应能用一个词或点头回答；这些病史帮助预判恶化，不只是贴严重度标签。沙丁胺醇可短暂引起咳嗽或声音更大，需与进气减少、疲竭或意识下降区分。快速恶化者需立即重评支持，不能规定非等每次雾化完；拒绝转运时也须依适当拒绝流程。

00:25:04.536 --> 00:25:46.296
The additional PR09 notes matter: never use a CPAP mask as a bag-mask ventilation interface, and do not delay indicated medication just to apply CPAP. An initial transient saturation fall does not justify ignoring clinical deterioration. The source names an extra 7-8 L/min when its connected nebulizer arrangement is used; this is accessory-specific guidance, not a universal pressure conversion or permission to exceed the pressure ceiling. Verify the actual kit and gas supply. A DNR or MOST does not by itself rule out CPAP for symptom relief; reconcile goals, consent and eligibility.
PR09补充注意也重要：不能把CPAP面罩当BVM接口，也不能为装CPAP拖延有指征药物。开始时短暂血氧下降，不代表可忽略临床恶化。来源在其连接雾化器配置中列额外7至8 L/分钟，这是附件特定指导，不是通用压力换算或超过压力上限许可，须核实际套件及气源。DNR或MOST本身不自动排除缓解症状的CPAP，但要结合目标、同意及资格。

00:25:46.296 --> 00:26:00.456
At a cycling rest area, a fifty-six-year-old with known obstructive disease is breathless with wheeze and marked accessory effort. Start the primary assessment and appropriate treatment while obtaining a brief history.
在骑行休息区，56岁已知阻塞病者气促喘鸣，辅助肌明显用力。应开始主要评估及适当治疗，同时简短问病史。

00:26:00.456 --> 00:26:12.792
After oxygen, saturation rises, but the patient becomes drowsier, takes shallower breaths and has less audible air entry. Those changes do not demonstrate recovery.
补氧后饱和度上升，但患者更嗜睡、呼吸更浅、进气声更少。这些变化不证明恢复。

00:26:12.792 --> 00:26:24.360
Name the threat as failing effective ventilation and possible exhaustion, while considering competing causes. Recheck airway, circulation and actual treatment delivery.
应指出威胁为有效通气失败及可能疲竭，同时考虑鉴别，重核气道、循环及真实治疗输送。

00:26:24.360 --> 00:26:35.184
Provide appropriate assisted support and escalation rather than applying CPAP to someone who no longer meets the functional screen. Do not wait for a confirmatory blood gas.
应给予适当辅助支持并升级，不能给已不符合功能筛查者上CPAP，也不能等血气确认。

00:26:35.184 --> 00:26:49.392
A seventy-four-year-old at a community workshop is awake with severe work, wet lung sounds and high initial pressure. Pulmonary edema is a leading concern, but the full assessment and differential still matter.
社区工作坊中，74岁者清醒、呼吸功严重、肺部湿音且初压高。肺水肿是主要怀疑，但完整评估及鉴别仍重要。

00:26:49.392 --> 00:27:00.696
Assume the complete CPAP screen is met and the actual trained device is used. Record the initial state, settings and treatment times while primary care continues.
假设完整CPAP筛查符合，并使用实际受训装置。主要照护持续时，记录初始状态、设定及治疗时间。

00:27:00.696 --> 00:27:09.816
Later the saturation is better, but pressure and responsiveness fall. A benefit in one variable does not make the overall treatment safe.
随后饱和度更好，血压和反应却下降。一项变量受益，不使整体治疗安全。

00:27:09.816 --> 00:27:24.312
Reassess the patient, device, pressure effect and alternative causes, stop unsafe support and use the appropriate rescue pathway. Report what changed rather than describing CPAP as successful from saturation alone.
应重评患者、设备、压力效应及其他原因，停止不安全支持并用适当救援路径。要报告变化，不能只凭饱和度称CPAP成功。

00:27:24.312 --> 00:27:36.528
If support appears to fail, look at the patient first and provide necessary rescue ventilation or oxygen. A prolonged equipment investigation must not leave the patient unsupported.
支持似失败时，先看患者并给必要救援通气或氧。不能长时间查设备，让患者无支持。

00:27:36.528 --> 00:27:46.944
Trace the oxygen source, regulator, set flow and available reserve. A sound of gas or a previously full cylinder is not a current supply check.
应追查氧源、调压器、设定流量及可用余量。有气声或先前满瓶，不算现在氧源检查。

00:27:46.944 --> 00:27:58.968
Follow the circuit to the patient, checking connections, valves, leaks and obstruction using the actual instructions. Do not improvise an unverified valve arrangement under pressure.
应沿回路到患者，依真实说明核连接、阀、漏气及阻塞。不能压力下自创未验证阀组合。

00:27:58.968 --> 00:28:10.680
After a correction, verify both equipment function and clinical response. Document the fault and action, and arrange appropriate equipment follow-up without losing patient care.
修正后，应验证设备功能及临床反应，记录故障行动，并在不丢失照护下安排设备后续。

00:28:10.680 --> 00:28:22.512
Begin a rehearsal by naming the current threat, leading mechanism and dangerous alternative. State the indication and every relevant exclusion before touching the pressure device.
演练开始先说当前威胁、首要机制及危险鉴别。碰正压设备前，应说明指征及每项相关排除。

00:28:22.512 --> 00:28:37.248
Identify actual equipment, oxygen supply and monitoring, then verbalize the starting setting, maximum and rescue plan. For medicine, state product, route, dose, unit and consultation gate.
应认清真实设备、氧源及监测，再口述起始、最高及救援计划。药物则说产品、途径、剂量、单位及咨询关卡。

00:28:37.248 --> 00:28:48.264
After the intervention, say what improved, what could worsen and what else the presentation could be. Use observed function instead of a declaration that the procedure is done.
干预后应说改善什么、可能坏什么、表现还可能是什么。用观察功能，不能只宣布操作完成。

00:28:48.264 --> 00:28:59.712
Rehearse a deterioration and stop the unsafe branch promptly. This prepares the reasoning for the school station; it does not substitute for observed hands-on device performance.
应演练一次恶化，及时停不安全分支。这准备学校站推理，不能替代被观察的实体设备表现。

00:28:59.712 --> 00:29:09.672
Start with who the patient is and why the respiratory problem is urgent. Give the baseline and current function, not just an asthma or COPD label.
先说患者是谁、呼吸问题为何紧急。要给基线及当前功能，不只哮喘或COPD名称。

00:29:09.672 --> 00:29:19.656
Report actual drug doses, routes and times, and the device, settings and pressure changes. Distinguish what was administered from what was only considered.
需报告真实剂量途径时间，以及设备、设定及压力变化，并区分已给与只考虑。

00:29:19.656 --> 00:29:32.592
Describe air movement, work, responsiveness, oxygenation and perfusion before and after treatment. Include any deterioration and why support was stopped or changed.
要描述治疗前后气流、功、反应、氧合灌注，包括恶化及为何停止或改变支持。

00:29:32.592 --> 00:29:44.832
End with current support, the next capability needed and a confirmed receiving plan. Preserve uncertainty honestly so the next team does not inherit a false final diagnosis.
最后给当前支持、下一所需能力及确认接收计划。应诚实保留不确定，避免下一团队继承错误定论。

00:29:44.832 --> 00:29:54.192
You should now explain why obstruction can cause air trapping and why saturation, rate and sound alone cannot establish adequate ventilation.
现在应能解释阻塞如何导致气体潴留，以及为何饱和度、频率或声音单独不能证明通气足够。

00:29:54.192 --> 00:30:05.160
Demonstrate the reasoning behind effective inhaled delivery and the checked local adult regimens. Keep pediatric, consultation and advanced-role differences visible.
应展示有效吸入给药及核对当地成人方案背后的推理，明确儿科、咨询及高级角色差异。

00:30:05.160 --> 00:30:14.232
Reconstruct the complete CPAP screen, device-linked titration and stop plan, then explain the separate PEEP indication and exclusions.
应重建完整CPAP筛查、依设备滴定及停止计划，再解释独立PEEP指征及排除。

00:30:14.232 --> 00:30:26.280
Use the bilingual reading and original cases to practise decisions, not recite fragments. The next workshop applies the same quality-first reasoning to complex twelve-lead findings.
应以中英阅读及原创病例练决定，而非背碎片。下一课把同样质量优先推理，用于复杂十二导联发现。
